  <prompt>
    This is a **coordination gate**, not an implementation task. W5 (tasks 051–054) edits `Services/Ai/` internals (OutputRouter dispositions, EventRules fan-out, a new JPS Action, DeliverComposite) that per [`projects/INDEX.md`](../../INDEX.md) are **SOLE-OWNED by `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2` (r2-core)**, which publishes seams under `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`. W5 MUST NOT fork those internals.

    Before ANY W5 implementation begins, you MUST: (1) run `/conflict-check` to detect active-PR overlap on `Services/Ai/`; (2) confirm with r2-core who owns the OutputRouter `record` + `notification` disposition legs and how R4 should complete them (extend via seam vs r2-core lands it vs coordinated hand-off); (3) confirm which `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams W5 consumes for record/notification routing, EventRules firing, and DeliverComposite; (4) document the agreed boundary in project notes. Tasks 051–054 are `&lt;blocked-by&gt;050&lt;/blocked-by&gt;` and MUST NOT start until this gate clears.

    If ownership is contested or the seams do not yet exist, this is a **real stop** — surface it per root CLAUDE.md §6 / §6.5, do NOT improvise by forking internals.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF coordination lead. Understands the `Services/Ai/` ownership model, the PublicContracts facade pattern (refined ADR-013), and the hot-path coordination registry (`projects/INDEX.md`). Authorized to open the escalation per CLAUDE.md §6.5 if a boundary conflict surfaces.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A written, agreed **W5 boundary** in `projects/email-communication-solution-r4/notes/w5-ai-coordination.md` that states: (a) `/conflict-check` result for `Services/Ai/`; (b) who lands OutputRouter `record`/`notification` disposition completion and how (seam vs fork-forbidden); (c) the exact `PublicContracts` seams tasks 051–054 will consume; (d) any escalation raised + its resolution path (A/B/C per §6.5). Once recorded and confirmed clear, tasks 051–054 are unblocked (status flips 🔲) and `TASK-INDEX.md` reflects the gate cleared.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per R4 CLAUDE.md "Hot-Path Coordination": r2-core is sole owner of `Services/Ai/` internals; also touching that surface: `spaarke-daily-update-service-r5`, `spaarkeai-compose-r2`, `chat-routing-redesign-r1`, `spaarke-ai-platform-unification-r6`. W1/W3 touch `Services/Communication/**` + new files (low overlap); W5 is the high-overlap wave. This gate exists to prevent a merge collision + duplicated OutputRouter work.

      FR-18 removes `NotSupportedException` in `DispositionRoutability.cs` (an r2-core-owned file) — the single most likely conflict point. Resolve ownership here before 051 touches it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/INDEX.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/OutputRouter/DispositionRoutability.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">GATE: tasks 051–054 MUST NOT start until this gate clears. This is `parallel-safe: false` and runs from the main session.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST run `/conflict-check` against `Services/Ai/` before any W5 code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">W5 consumes `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; do NOT inject AI-internal types (`IOpenAiClient`, `IPlaybookService`) directly; do NOT fork `Services/Ai/` internals.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §6/§6.5">If ownership/seams are contested or missing, STOP and escalate (Human Input Required / ADR Conflict Resolution). Silent forking is forbidden.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`projects/INDEX.md` is the authoritative ownership registry — consult it, and update the R4 hot-path entry if the boundary shifts.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/INDEX.md</file>
