  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `projects/INDEX.md` hot-path entries for `Services/Ai/` — confirm r2-core sole ownership + the other touching projects.</step>
    <step order="2">Run `/conflict-check` (conflict-check skill) scoped to `Services/Ai/`; capture the active-PR overlap report.</step>
    <step order="3">Inventory the existing `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` seams; identify which cover: OutputRouter record/notification routing, `EventRulesService.FireAsync`, and `DeliverComposite`. Note gaps.</step>
    <step order="4">Read `DispositionRoutability.cs` to see the current `NotSupportedException` legs FR-18 must complete; determine whether completion is a seam extension or an internal edit (the latter requires r2-core agreement).</step>
    <step order="5">Coordinate with r2-core (record the exchange): confirm (a) who lands OutputRouter `record`/`notification` completion, (b) the seams 051–054 consume, (c) whether any r2-core change must merge first.</step>
    <step order="6">Write `projects/email-communication-solution-r4/notes/w5-ai-coordination.md` capturing the agreed boundary (a–d from `&lt;goal&gt;`), including any escalation + resolution path.</step>
    <step order="7">If a boundary conflict is unresolved, STOP and surface per §6/§6.5 (Human Input Required / ADR Conflict) — do NOT unblock 051–054.</step>
    <step order="8">If clear: flip tasks 051–054 status 🔲 in `TASK-INDEX.md`, mark 050 ✅ (gate cleared), and note the cleared boundary in `current-task.md`. Advance to task 051.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect INDEX.md, PublicContracts, DispositionRoutability.cs</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Detect active-PR overlap on Services/Ai/</tool>
    <tool name="write">Record the agreed boundary in notes</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
