  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`/conflict-check` was run against `Services/Ai/` and its result is recorded in the coordination note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note states who lands OutputRouter `record`/`notification` completion and how (no internal fork by W5).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The note enumerates the exact `PublicContracts` seams tasks 051–054 will consume (or records missing-seam escalation).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Either 051–054 are unblocked (gate cleared) OR an escalation is raised per §6/§6.5 and 051–054 remain blocked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `Services/Ai/` internal code was forked or edited in this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This gate is the single biggest schedule risk in W5 (per plan High-Risk / Watch Items). Treat "boundary unclear" as a legitimate stop — the cost of a merge collision on OutputRouter is far higher than the cost of waiting for r2-core.

    Also touching `Services/Ai/`: `spaarke-daily-update-service-r5`, `spaarkeai-compose-r2`, `chat-routing-redesign-r1`, `spaarke-ai-platform-unification-r6` — include them in the conflict scan if `/conflict-check` surfaces their PRs.
